            "review_title": "Review at Banh Xeo 335",
            "review_text": "IVI4CS\nMarbella, Spain323 contributions\n0\nCrunch…\nJan 2026 • Couples\nSo this is a spot tucked away in a little alley, a really typical place a bit outside the center of Saigon. There are several of them, but this one is particularly good and clean for a street food stall. They serve a Vietnamese pancake\n- Bánh xèo đặc biệt (pancake)\n- Bánh khọt (mini pancake) \nthat’s made with equal parts rice flour and water. \nFor the big one, the batter is poured into a very hot wok, and then they add pork, shrimp, bean sprouts, and also some mung bean sprouts. They crack an egg in there as well and fold the pancake into a half-moon shape.\nThe small\nOne is the same batter but with less topping and is deep fried\nFor the small ones, when you eat them, you add a little coconut cream on top for a sweet touch. The larger ones you can dip into traditional fish sauces or other condiments. It comes with a little basket full of herbs: Thai basil, coriander, mustard leaves, lettuce, mint, all these intense flavors. You take a piece of lettuce or mustard leaf, add the herbs, cut a bit of the omelet, and roll it up like a little spring roll to eat with your fingers. It’s super tasty, crunchy and perfect as a starter or appetizer to begin the evening. It’s not expensive, it’s quick, the people are very friendly, and it’s just super, super typical.\nRead more\nWritten January 19, 2026",
