            "review_title": "Review at Banh Xeo 335",
            "review_text": "Nomadicus\nBuffalo, NY720 contributions\n0\nA Benchmark First Bite at Bánh Xèo Miền Tây\nOct 2025 • Friends\nWe stopped at Bánh Xèo Miền Tây as part of a Ho Chi Minh City food tour, and in hindsight, it was the perfect place for a first introduction to both bánh xèo and bánh khọt. First impressions matter, and this one set the bar high.\n\nAt the time, I didn’t yet have much context. Since then, I’ve eaten plenty of versions around the city and beyond, and I can say with confidence that this remains one of the best. The bánh xèo arrives exactly as it should: audibly crisp, generously filled with shrimp, mung beans, and enoki, and paired with the usual vibrant basket of fresh greens and herbs that turns each bite into a build-your-own balance of texture and brightness.\n\nAs good as the bánh xèo is, the bánh khọt truly shines here. Crisp-edged, rich, and deeply satisfying, it was the dish that lingered in memory long after the table cleared. If there’s a reason to return, this is it.\n\nService only strengthens the experience. The staff is warm, welcoming, and genuinely eager to share the business and process with all interested in seeing the behind the scenes, which makes the meal feel both approachable and celebratory.\n\nWhether it’s your first encounter with these Vietnamese staples or your tenth, Bánh Xèo Miền Tây delivers with consistency, generosity, and hospitality. It’s a place that teaches you what these dishes are supposed to taste like, and then does it better than most.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nIf with a tour guide, you'll be fine. Otherwise, be prepared with some Vietnamese in your vocabulary or be prepared to use google translate\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 7, 2025",
